we were able to kick out a couple a year and&nbsp;
again the home video market was so was so big you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:36.560
were able to get territories to put up a lot of&nbsp;
money around the globe for the home video market&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:42.960
tv rights foreign theatrical things have changed&nbsp;
substantially I find it easier to make movies now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:46.720
because we're able to make movies for a lot less I&nbsp;
mean we're shooting all those movies on Panavision&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:52.320
35 millimeter cameras that camera package to&nbsp;
rent that film to to buy and process and tell us&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:58.560
any and convert to video digital format so you can&nbsp;
cut it on your AVIDS which back then cost $180,000&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:06.160
it movies were expensive back then we&nbsp;
weren't making them for cheap it's just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:12.080
and we were doing independent films and I cringe&nbsp;
today when I hear about independent movies that&nbsp;&nbsp;

